{% comment %}
  Resolves the colour scheme a first-time visitor gets, into `site_theme`.

  Two places need it and they must not disagree: _layouts/default.html writes it
  on <html> so the server-rendered page is already the right scheme, and
  head.html's early script rewrites it only when the visitor has chosen one
  before. If those two ever gave different answers the page would flash the
  wrong scheme before the script ran, which is the whole reason the attribute is
  written server-side in the first place.

  default_theme in _config.yml decides. The Christmas theme still falls back to
  dark on its own, so the seasonal flag keeps working if default_theme is ever
  cleared.
{% endcomment %}
{% if site.default_theme == 'dark' or site.default_theme == 'light' %}
  {% assign site_theme = site.default_theme %}
{% elsif site.christmas_theme %}
  {% assign site_theme = 'dark' %}
{% else %}
  {% assign site_theme = 'light' %}
{% endif %}
